    <string name="app_name">Snoozemo</string>

    <!--
      Phase 1 debug screen only. This copy is scaffolding for a device check, not
      product copy: it is replaced by onboarding and settings in later phases and
      never reaches a release, so it is deliberately not translated and has not
      been through the propose-copy-in-chat step.
    -->
    <!--
      The two setup rows. Each is a whole tappable target, so the sentence that
      names the problem is the thing you tap — the status line used to be inert
      text beside a separate button (`TODO.md` Phase 2).

      The action line is a separate string on purpose: the two permissions are
      not the same kind of thing, and the row is where that has to be legible.
      Do Not Disturb access is a Settings toggle, so the user leaves the app and
      comes back (SPEC.md §5.2); `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` is a runtime prompt that
      appears in place — until the system stops showing it, after which Settings
      is the only route left and the row says so instead.
    -->
